<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/19th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Treaty · Peace</p><h1 class="enc-title">Treaties of Tilsit</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1807</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Peace of Tilsit · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/war-of-the-fourth-coalition">War of the Fourth Coalition</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Treaties of Tilsit were signed in July 1807 by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon">Napoleon</a> with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alexander-i-of-russia">Alexander I of Russia</a> and Frederick William III of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-prussia">Prussia</a>, after the French victory at Friedland. Prussia lost about half its territory: its Polish lands formed the Duchy of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/warsaw">Warsaw</a>, and Danzig became a free city under French control. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a> joined the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/continental-system">Continental System</a> against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a>, and the settlement marked the peak of Napoleon's power in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/treaties-of-tilsit.jpg" alt="Treaties of Tilsit" width="320" height="249" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Adolphe Roehn · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Tilsitz_1807.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
